# Pairs with RNoStrandedPrepare. Regression check for issue #4508, fixed by
# #4553. The receiver settles a re-shipped pre-cut prepare against the decision
# row the export carries (#4510), so it can only do so for a saga whose
# decision the origin still stores. Before #4553 the origin purged a
# forgotten saga's decision row on retention alone, while its WAL could still
# re-ship a prepare of the saga: the export then carried no verdict, the
# receiver had nothing to settle against, and a retained prepare whose
# terminal was trimmed was staged with no terminal behind it. Since #4553 the
# row is kept until the WAL has trimmed every prepare of the saga, which
# OriginPurge states. The replay filter (#4533) now also withholds a purged
# saga's re-shipped prepare, so the guard is defence in depth: the mutation
# removes both, and either alone keeps RNoStrandedPrepare.
MODULE: RNoStrandedPrepareDedupeOverPurgedDecision
TARGET: RNoStrandedPrepare
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the origin purges a forgotten saga's decision while a prepare of it is still retained, as before #4553, and no replay filter withholds it
PERTURBS: OriginPurge
BOUNDS: LossPath = 0, JoinStart = 1, Shape = 0

--- FIND
       ELSE /\ ~Held
            /\ CrossTreeAcked
            /\ \/ ~rconn
               \/ detached
               \/ ~\E p \in outbox : p.type = "prep" /\ Aff(p)
            /\ ptrim' = TRUE
            /\ outbox' = {r \in outbox : r.type # "prep" \/ ~Aff(r)}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the decision is purged while a prepare is still retained.
       ELSE /\ ~Held
            /\ CrossTreeAcked
            /\ UNCHANGED <<outbox, ptrim>>
--- END
--- FIND
ReplayShips == ~filt \/ FirstSight = "ship"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: and no replay filter withholds the purged saga.
ReplayShips == TRUE
--- END
